# Supabase — same project as apps/web, patient role JWT
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Platform API (apps/api) base URL
# Local dev: http://localhost:3002
# Staging: https://api-dev.osteojp.pt
# Production: https://api.osteojp.pt
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.osteojp.pt

# App URL — THE PORTAL IS ON A CUSTOM DOMAIN, AND IT IS `portal.`, NOT `patient.`
#
# CORRECTED 2026-09-07. Everything this block said before was true when written.
#
# `portal.osteojp.pt` IS LIVE, on cname.vercel-dns.com, serving /marcacao with a
# 200. Measured by dig and curl on 2026-09-07, not read off a dashboard.
#
# `osteojp-portal.vercel.app` IS THE SAME DEPLOYMENT, not a preview: both hosts
# returned byte-identical HTML that day,
# sha256 003a8d9647f2e2b5f5edd85dbd6ec392ef2c112a553212bcb7a037ffef1697db.
# It is the project's production alias; a PREVIEW url carries a deployment hash
# in the hostname. Either host is safe to open.
#
# `patient.osteojp.pt` STILL DOES NOT RESOLVE and never became the portal. It
# was the planned name and the name that shipped is `portal.`. This file named
# `patient.` until 2026-08-12 and then named the vercel.app host until today;
# both were correct at the time, and the second one outlived its reason — a
# reader in 2026-09 concluded the portal had no custom domain at all.
#
# THE VALUE BELOW IS THE EXAMPLE, NOT THE DEPLOYMENT. The live value lives on
# the Vercel project (osteojp-portal) and is the only authority; confirm it
# there before a sitting. Since both hosts serve the same deployment, either
# value works today, and the custom domain is the one to prefer because it is
# the one a patient is given.
#
# NOTE the staff platform is app.osteojp.pt, also live on cname.vercel-dns.com.
# The two hosts now follow the SAME pattern; earlier revisions of this file
# warned that they did not, and that warning is retired.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://portal.osteojp.pt
